  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Several garment factories in Gazipur, Bangladesh have declared holidays as minimum wage protests continue, and clashes have erupted between workers and police along the Dhaka–Mymensingh Highway.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-22:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 15 November, protests continued despite warnings from the BGMEA and the BKMEA to enforce \"no work, no pay\" closures under Section 13 (1) of the Bangladesh Labour Act, 2006.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1387085398:72"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The workers are demanding that the sector's minimum monthly wage rise from ৳12,500 (US$100) to ৳30,000 (US$240).",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1387085398:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Inflation in Bangladesh was 8.8% in 2025, down from 10.5% in 2024.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG:BD"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The economy grew 3.5% in 2025, and unemployment stood at 3.8%.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG:BD",
        "wb:SL.UEM.TOTL.ZS:BD"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "Across South Asia, Bangladesh's 8.8% inflation compares with a median of 2.7%, and Bangladesh has the highest figure in the region.",
      "cites": [
        "wb:FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG:region:south-asia"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:00:57Z",
      "text": "The Business Standard and The Daily Star reported on the story.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-22:5",
        "wiki:2026-11-22:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:01:05Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined it: “Clashes erupt across France in another night of protest”",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:3a8c8b4e1fd2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:01:12Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined it: “Europe sees new protests over rising costs, inequality and public services”",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:a1d144e53fad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-22T00:01:21Z",
      "text": "Sources include Wikipedia, Wikimedia pageviews, Wikidata and World Bank Open Data, and each caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
      "cites": [
